# Firearm Bolt Catch Mechanism

## Formal Patent Description

A firearm mechanism comprising:

a bolt catch (**10**) formed of a first rail (**12**) and a second rail (**14**), said first rail (**12**) and said second rail (**14**) being disposed in substantially parallel spaced relation;

a bridge member (**16**) integrally connecting said first rail (**12**) to said second rail (**14**), thereby defining a unitary catch assembly;

said first rail (**12**) having a projection (**18**) extending outwardly therefrom, said projection (**18**) being configured to arrest rearward movement of a breech component;

a cartridge feeder (**20**) operatively associated with said bolt catch (**10**), said cartridge feeder (**20**) being disposed for selective engagement with said projection (**18**);

wherein, upon discharge of a final cartridge from said firearm, said cartridge feeder (**20**) is urged upwardly into abutting contact with said projection (**18**) of said first rail (**12**), whereby said bolt catch (**10**) is displaced to a position retaining a breech (**22**) of said firearm in an open configuration.

